today bring you the latest on  our vaccination program and our work to  get  even more people protected from this  deadly  disease we've come a long way  since we gave the world's first  clinically authorized vaccine  just over six months ago since that very  special  day we've now given a first dose  to 82 percent of all adults  in the united kingdom and today  i can confirm we've reached the  milestone of  three in five three and five of all  adults  getting the protection of a second dose  because we've been able to move at such  a pace  any adult in the uk can now book  their first dose in the two days  after we opened our booking system to  anyone over the age of 18  there were six appointments being booked  every second and i've been  absolutely thrilled to see videos of  young people  coming forward at some of our major  vaccination events  last weekend and i'm sure they'll be  doing the same this coming  weekend the enthusiasm  is making a huge difference  we've already given first doses  to almost half of all 25  to 29 year olds in england  and only a week after the program  opened to all adults  on friday one-third one-third  of people aged between 18 and 24  have had their first dose to all of the  young people  who have stepped up i want to say a huge  thank you  you've protected yourself you've  protected your families  and you've protected your communities  because the one thing you know we know  is the vaccines are making the real  difference the vaccines are  our way out of this pandemic the latest  data  show that the vaccination program has  already saved over 14  000 lives and i can share with you  that now it has prevented over 44  500 44 thousand five hundred  hospitalizations  in england alone that's two and a half  thousand  hospitalizations prevented in the past  two weeks and when you look into the  makeup  of hospital admissions you can clearly  see  our vaccination program is working  can i have the first slide please in  january  people over 65 made up the vast  majority of hospital admissions  that is why we vaccinated them early  in the program if you look at the most  recent data  they show that now they make up less  than a  third so when we look at the  uh protection that the vaccines  deliver it is clear from that slide  that it's clean extremely effective  especially with two days  against the delta variant the recently  published  uh data from public health england  looked at around  500 hospital admissions with the delta  variant  of these admissions 324  patients so over 60 percent were  unvaccinated  87 had received only one dose  of a vaccine and 40 had received two  doses  so fewer than one in ten people in  hospital  with the delta variant had received two  doses  this really does show the importance of  getting the jab and critically  getting that second dose so our mission  is now to get as many people protected  as we can and to protect them  as quickly as we can last week  we took the difficult but i think  essential decision  to pause step four in our roadmap for  four weeks  with a review of the data after two  weeks and we will absolutely  have that review and share the data with  the nation  we're going to use these four weeks to  give our nhs  that bit more time so that we can get  those remaining jabs  in arms of those who really do  need them so let me give you an example  of why it is so  important two weeks ago there were over  two million  two million people over the age of 50  in england who'd had a first dose but  not their second dose now  that number two weeks later is nine  hundred thousand  down from two million to nine hundred  thousand this pause  has and saved thousands of lives  and will continue to do so by allowing  us  to get more of the second doses  into arms of those most vulnerable to  covert before the restrictions are eased  further we've also reduced the interval  from first to second jab for over 40s  to eight weeks and i would urge everyone  watching  if you are over 40 come forward  and have your second jab take the  opportunity  and get the second jab early you can do  that  by going online at the national booking  service or calling one one  night we've seen phenomenal uptake  and enthusiasm for our vaccination  program so far the united kingdom has  won  the highest rates of vaccine confidence  in the world  nine in ten people nine and ten of all  adults say they've either taken the  vaccine  or that they want to take the vaccine  it's something we can all be proud of  but it is no  accident ladies and gentlemen  we got here because  we have actively  and nikki will be very much  explaining exactly what how we've done  that gone out  to really address people's genuine  concerns  and have open two-way conversations  about these vaccines and how safe they  are and how important they are to saving  lives and because we've worked with  local communities  on the design of the vaccination program  so we can deliver it  in a way that works for people in a  place they trust by  people they trust our vaccination  program has been  delivered in the community by the  community and for  the community and it's been a brilliant  brilliant  experience to see vaccinations being  given in churches synagogues gudoras  mosques temples and many other pillars  of the community  all across the whole of the united  kingdom and to see the determined  effort of the brilliant people  real partners on the ground to reach  communities where  take-up has been lower this concerted  community-led  effort i believe has truly paid off and  we're seeing  real positive results so if you look at  the latest data from the office for  national statistics the ons  vaccine hesitancy has halved in the past  few months among  black and black british people since  february and it's halved among asian  and asian british people two in the same  period this is real progress  but we know there's more much more to do  as we look to tackle and take on those  final steps those hard yards  on the road to recovery we need to make  sure  as many people are protected as possible  so we're intensifying doubling down our  efforts  to get more people to come forward and  we're seeing real results  in places like bolton and of course in  the northwest  and elsewhere we're honing on areas  where uptake is lower for example in  london  where the percentage of first doses is  slightly behind  the other areas in the united kingdom  the london team is doing  an incredible job and i can confirm  today that we're supporting them we're  supporting them with a london  summit that will take place on friday  bringing together senior officials  the nhs in london the mayor of london  clinical experts and community leaders  from across the capital  so that we can see what has worked and  how we can learn from it and  scale it and of course focus on how we  make sure we really do boost  that crucial uptake in the crucial few  weeks before the 19th  of july thanks to our vaccination  program our incredible nhs  this country is getting a little bit  safer  every day whatever your age  whatever your background the vaccine  will protect you it'll protect your  family and  all the people that you care about so  please come forward  and get both doses  so we can take that final step on the  road  to recovery
 

